course: dictionary
lesson: 14732
title: Prohibit: when a rule says no
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To prohibit something is to forbid it officially, usually by a rule or a law. Signs and notices use this word a lot. «Swimming prohibited» on a pool gate means nobody may swim there.
explain: Prohibit can also mean to make something impossible. «The cost prohibits us from going» means the price is too high, so we cannot go. Ask yourself: is there a rule, or is something stopping it? Either way, prohibit means it cannot happen.
explain: Prohibit is a formal word. In speech, most children say «not allowed» or «banned», and that is fine. In notices, rule books and exams, you will meet prohibited. Look for the clue phrases: prohibited from, strictly prohibited, prohibited items.
fact: Prohibit means to officially forbid something, or to make it impossible.
fact: «Smoking is prohibited» means a rule says that no one may smoke here.
fact: «Strictly prohibited» means there are no exceptions: it is not allowed at all.
fact: «Prohibited items» are things a rule says you must not bring, such as at an airport.
fact: Synonyms: ban, forbid and not allowed mean much the same, but prohibit is the formal choice.
exercise: «Swimming prohibited» is written on the pool gate. What does this sign mean? | You may swim here if you are careful | The pool is very big | Swimming lessons start at noon | *You are not allowed to swim here
exercise: «The cost prohibits us from going to the museum.» What does prohibits mean here? | Makes the museum free | Tells us to hurry | Invites us to a party | *Makes it impossible for us to go
exercise: «Phones are strictly prohibited during exams.» Copy the word that shows there are no exceptions. | phones | during | exams | *strictly
test: «Dogs are prohibited from the beach in summer.» What does prohibited mean? | Lost | Very happy | Sold cheaply | *Officially forbidden
test: Which word is the formal way of saying «not allowed»? | *Prohibited | Gentle | Pretty | Sleepy
exam: Ravi reads «Prohibited items must stay in the locker.» What does prohibited mean? | Lost property | Allowed to be carried everywhere | *Not allowed, so they must stay in the locker | Very expensive
